.Dd September 24, 2026
.Dt DITTO 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ditto
.Nd copy files and directories, and create and extract archive files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar options
.Ar src
.Op Ar src Ar ...
.Ar dst
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility copies
.Ar src
files and directories to
.Ar dst .
By default it copies the contents of a source directory rather than the
directory itself, preserves resource data and extended attributes, and
copies symbolic links as symbolic links.
.Pp
If
.Ar src
is a directory, its contents are copied.
If
.Ar src
is a file or symbolic link it is copied as that file.
Multiple
.Ar src
arguments copy each source into the destination directory.
.Pp
With
.Fl c ,
.Nm
creates an archive at
.Ar dst
instead of copying.
The default archive format is CPIO (odc format).
Only one source may be given with
.Fl c ,
and unlike a straight copy the archive embeds the basename of the source
so it can be recreated on extraction.
.Pp
With
.Fl x ,
.Fl c
is inverted and
.Ar src
is an archive from which entries are extracted into the destination
directory.
The archive format is chosen automatically unless
.Fl k
is given.
.Pp
The following options are supported:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl h , -help
Print usage information and exit.
.It Fl v
Print a status line for each source processed.
.It Fl V
Print a status line for every file processed.
.It Fl c
Create an archive at
.Ar dst
(CPIO format unless
.Fl k
is given).
.It Fl x
Extract archives instead of copying.
.It Fl z
Use gzip compression when creating a CPIO archive.
.It Fl j
Use bzip2 compression when creating a CPIO archive.
.It Fl k
Create the archive in PKZip format.
.It Fl keepParent
Embed the parent directory name of
.Ar src
in the archive so that extraction recreates it.
.El
.Pp
Extended attribute (AppleDouble) data is stored next to each entry both
when copying to an archive and when extracting, and
.Fl z /
.Fl j
wrappers are byte-identical to the corresponding output of Apple's
ditto for ordinary directory trees.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width DITTOABORT
.It Ev DITTONORSRC
Do not preserve any filesystem metadata.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mkbom 1 ,
.Xr lsbom 1
.Sh HISTORY
This implementation is a clean-room rewrite of the classic
.Nm
utility.
Only the core option set listed above is implemented; the full
.BomCopier
option space
.Pq Xo
.Fl Fl arch ,
.Fl Fl bom ,
.Fl Fl lang ,
.Fl Fl rsr c Ns -family
.Xc
is not implemented yet.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An LibreDarwin